## (2b) root cause of MONO-MV-02, measured (headless Chrome probe, :5629, b9f5195)

GEOM @390: #hero position:relative, top 0, height 1607.11, docHeight 19667, innerHeight 844
  → at scrollY 0 the hero's intersection ratio is 844/1607 = 0.525, above the
    observer's 0.35 threshold, so pastHero is false and the dock is unpainted.
    (The COMMENT's premise — "the ratio can never approach 0.35" — does not hold
    at 390: the hero is 1.90 viewports tall, not "far taller".)
  → the ratio drops below 0.35 at scrollY ≈ 1045, so the dock paints while the
    hero's last 562px is still on screen. That band is at the TOP of the
    viewport (hero bottom at y=562) and the dock is bottom-anchored (launcher
    top y ≈ 756), so nothing of the launcher touches the hero. G-E2 holds.

Dock state through the spec's own scroll loop @390:
  step 0: scrollY 1266  opacity 0.992969  data-past-hero="true"  → loop breaks
  label: text "Ask Mini Vic", composited opacity 1, rgb(205,205,205) on rgb(10,10,10)
  → every label assertion passes. The label half is NOT the failure.

Dock opacity after window.scrollTo(0, 0), sampled by rAF:
  computed transition on .minivic-dock = "opacity 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)"
  @390  t≈0 op=1 past=true | t≈100 op=1 past=null | t≈200 op=0.0792 | t≈300 op=0
  @640  t≈0 op=1 past=null | t≈100 op=1 past=null | t≈200 op=0.0312 | t≈300 op=0

  The fade cannot begin until the IntersectionObserver has re-reported #hero and
  React has re-rendered with pastHero false (~1 frame + a render), and then runs
  for 300ms. Observer/render latency + 300ms transition ≈ the spec's own 400ms
  wait, so the single sample lands ON the boundary of a still-falling curve.
  ROOT CAUSE: TEST — the instrument samples the withdrawal, not the settled state.
  The product reaches opacity 0 over the fold at both widths, within ~300ms.
